  "The room list of the slice, one entry per room, in the game-designer's form (kiln, templates/room-brief.md explains every key as prose).",
  "game, start, hub: the ids. installs: a kit carried from one room and granted at another (surgery at the hub): carried -> found -> at -> gives.",
  "roster: every enemy the rooms place, by cast id, with the intensity the pacing curve weighs it at (a design claim about how hard it is, 1 for a grunt, 6 for the boss).",
  "rooms[].id: permanent, it lands in saves. name: what the sign says. style: the dressing family the level-artist keys on (optional). teaches: one verb or system id from design.md.",
  "rooms[].doors: the rooms this one connects to; symmetric. holds: what the player wants or reads, typed: item:<id>, hack:<id>, ability:<kit>, npc:<id>, quest_item:<id>, save, hp_up, ram_up, tease, notice, grate:<id>, breach_door:<id>, lift.",
  "rooms[].grants: the kit ids the room gives; each is a verb's kit in design.md or an installs[].carried, and each kit is granted in exactly one room. requires: kit ids needed to pass or use what the room gates; the level-designer proves them.",
  "rooms[].enemies: cast id -> count. rest: a breath (a save or an npc, no enemies). cell, size: filled by the level-designer once the district is laid out; the design leaves them out.",
  "rooms[].brief: story (the sentence the concept is prompted from), light (every source as 'what: colour, warm|cold|hot'), left (the props, in order), way_out, window (what it looks onto, or none), eye (the three stops the light budget is measured against)."
